{
  "id": "28726_agaru",
  "headword": "{揚|あ}がる",
  "reading": "あがる",
  "romaji": "agaru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to be deep-fried; to come out crispy",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be deep-fried; to come out (well) fried",
      "explanation": "For food being deep-fried to finish cooking, especially with a desirably crisp result. The intransitive partner of {揚|あ}げる."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28726_agaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{天|てん}ぷらがカラッと{揚|あ}がった。",
      "english": "The tempura came out crispy.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28726_agaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{油|あぶら}の{温度|おんど}が{高|たか}いと、すぐに{揚|あ}がる。",
      "english": "If the oil temperature is high, things fry quickly.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28726_agaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{衣|ころも}がきつね{色|いろ}に{揚|あ}がったら{油|あぶら}から{取|と}り{出|だ}してください。",
      "english": "Once the batter has fried to a golden brown, take it out of the oil.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Intransitive verb describing food finishing the deep-frying process. Often paired with adverbs that describe the texture or color of the result.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- カラッと{揚|あ}がる: to fry up crispy\n- きつね{色|いろ}に{揚|あ}がる: to fry to a golden brown\n- うまく{揚|あ}がる: to come out well\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {上|あ}がる (00615): to go up — the most common あがる\n- あがる (17309): to be nervous; to lose one's composure\n\nTRANSITIVE PAIR:\n- {揚|あ}げる: to deep-fry — used when the cook is the focus",
